+Use ``--strict`` to create a `STRICT table
+<https://www.sqlite.org/stricttables.html>`__ (requires SQLite 3.37 or higher)::
+
+    $ sqlite-utils create-table mydb.db mytable id integer name text --strict
+
+The ``insert`` and ``upsert`` commands also accept ``--strict`` when they create
+a new table.
+
+You can pass as many column-name column-type pairs as you like. Valid types are
+``integer``, ``text``, ``float``, ``blob``, ``real`` and ``any``. ``real`` and
+``any`` are especially useful with strict tables.
 
