+The configuration options that can be specified in this way are ``pk``, ``foreign_keys``, ``column_order``, ``not_null``, ``defaults``, ``batch_size``, ``hash_id``, ``alter``, ``ignore``, ``replace``, ``extracts``, ``conversions``, ``columns`` and ``strict``. These are all documented below.
+
+Strict tables
+=============
+
+SQLite 3.37 and higher supports `STRICT tables
+<https://www.sqlite.org/stricttables.html>`__. Create one by passing
+``strict=True`` to ``db.create_table()``, ``table.create()``, or to an insert or
+upsert method that creates a new table::
+
+    db["creatures"].insert(
+        {"name": "Cleo", "age": 3},
+        strict=True,
+    )
+
+The ``table.strict`` property reports whether an existing table is strict.
 
